From 17a67027da8f6361e1867cb842a67e02f679c5f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:48:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 272/272] ASoC: codecs: mt6369: Add the headphone downlink

Add the MT6369's audio DAC and headphone driver: an AIF1 playback
stream over MTKAIF, the downlink digital clocks, SDM and negative charge
pump, the decoder LDOs and NV regulator as DAPM supplies, and an HP Mux
that runs MediaTek's headphone power-up and power-down sequences. The
register sequences are from MediaTek's GPLv2 mt6369.c. The structure
follows mt6359.c.

Headphone Volume sets the driver's analog gain, -10 dB to +8 dB in 1 dB
steps, ramped while it plays. The line-out, receiver and DC trim paths
of the vendor driver are left out: on the Jolla Phone (2026) the
earpiece and speakers are on the AW88271s, and the headphones are the
only analog output, through the HL5280 USB-C switch.

Tested on the JP2601 with nothing plugged into USB-C:
- DAPM brings up and powers down the whole path (AIF1RX, DACs, NCP,
  SDM, NV regulator, HP Mux, Headphone L/R) for a DL0 stream on ADDA,
  with no errors.
- The AW88271s stay off while it plays.
- Capture and the MTKAIF calibration are unchanged.
No headset has been on it yet, so the analog output is not verified.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/mt6369.c | 525 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 sound/soc/codecs/mt6369.h |  98 +++++++
 2 files changed, 623 insertions(+)

